00 held in the company’s shares over the years it covers at $94.12 at the end of FY2026, and $256.61 for the peer group the company chose.","cites":["CRM.pay.tsr.2026","CRM.pay.peerTsr.2026"]},{"topic":"backlog","text":"Remaining performance obligations - revenue under contract that was not yet recognised - were $72.4 billion at the end of FY2026, against $63.4 billion a year earlier. That is 174.4% of FY2026 revenue (computed from two filed figures).","cites":["CRM.rpo.2026","CRM.rpo.2025","CRM.revenue.2026"]},{"topic":"backlog","text":"Deferred revenue was $24.3 billion at the end of FY2026 (tagged ContractWithCustomerLiabilityCurrent), against $20.7 billion a year earlier.","cites":["CRM.deferred.2026","CRM.deferred.2025"]},{"topic":"people","text":"The latest annual report gives the workforce as 83,334 in its own words. FY2026 revenue works out to about $498,000 for each (computed from one filed figure and the number in that sentence).","cites":["CRM.q.employees","CRM.revenue.2026"]},{"topic":"flags","text":"The FY2026 annual report tags restructuring charges of $586 million, after $461 million in FY2025.","cites":["CRM.restructuring.2026","CRM.restructuring.2025"]},{"topic":"debt","text":"At the end of FY2026 the balance sheet carried $7.3 billion in cash and cash equivalents and $2.2 billion in short-term investments, and $14.4 billion of debt as tagged (LongTermDebtNoncurrent + LongTermDebtCurrent). Debt less cash and short-term investments was $4.9 billion (computed from four filed figures).","cites":["CRM.cash.2026","CRM.sti.2026","CRM.debtLong.2026","CRM.debtCurrent.2026"]}]},"fin":{"CRM":{"insiders":{"from":"2025-11-23","to":"2026-11-23","complete":true,"listed":99,"read":99,"other":0,"failed":0,"odd":0,"people":[["Kirk David Blair","Director"],["Conway Craig","Director"],["ALBER LAURA","Director"],["KROES NEELIE","Director"],["Morfit G Mason and ValueAct Holdings, L.P. and ValueAct Capital Master Fund, L.P. and VA Partners I, LLC and ValueAct Capital Man